    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** headlining the roster as our most potent offensive threat. Scoring a 67.96, **Junior Caminero** benefits from a premium spot in the three-hole and a favorable matchup against the right-handed Cabrera, despite neutral park factors. Close behind is **Casey Schmitt** (63.11), who presents a high-upside play; while his raw base projection is modest, his score is bolstered by a +11% dynamic platoon advantage and a notable +5% boost from wind blowing out at the stadium. Similarly, **Kazuma Okamoto** (64.53) remains a high-floor anchor, leveraging a significant +19% SP skill advantage against Quantrill to maximize his expected production in the cleanup spot.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, prioritizing the 40.0 efficiency floor to preserve game caps. **Carson Benge** represents the most difficult cut of the day, finishing at 37.86. Despite a favorable lineup position, his score was suppressed by a difficult matchup against the southpaw Mayza and a -19% SP skill penalty, leaving him just shy of the threshold. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of **Yordan Alvarez** and **Christian Yelich**, who remain unavailable, and we are tracking **Hyeseong Kim**\u2019s development with the Oklahoma City Comets, keeping him stashed for future utility.\n\nRisk management is central to today\u2019s deployment, particularly regarding **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. His score of 47.62 is heavily impacted by a -15% platoon penalty against the left-handed Harrison and a -14% SP skill mismatch. While we are starting him to chase his elite speed potential, his efficiency is currently on the low end of our active spectrum. We are also wary of **Luke Raley**, who, despite a solid score of 55.42, faces a slight drag due to a catcher-driven adjustment for stolen base attempts, though he remains a viable option given his platoon strength. We continue to hold **Rece Hinds**, **Zac Veen**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, **Jose Fernandez**, and **Pedro Ramirez** in reserve as we navigate the volatile 2026 campaign.",
